From b3763477b2298b337c8921db80cd87e66ccc35bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:31:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync fake: release coerces like releaseTask
 (JS Number()/String(), ?? defaults) (PR #2199 review nits)

Follow-up to exact-head review 5891002346 on PR #2199. FakeService/FakeHub release now
reads its inputs the way hermes-hub worker/src/transitions.ts releaseTask does:

1. _js_to_number is ECMAScript Number(): ASCII digits only (\d took U+0663, which
   the Board reads as NaN; float() also took "1_000"), trimmed of StrWhiteSpaceChar
   (TAB VT FF ZWNBSP, Zs, LF CR LS PS) instead of str.strip() (which strips
   U+001C-U+001F/U+0085 and keeps U+FEFF), unsigned 0x/0o/0b literals, and arrays
   through String() ([] -> 0, ["3"] -> 3). The old out-of-scope caveat is gone.
2. block_kind is checked as String(op.block_kind ?? "transient"), so ["transient"]
   is accepted as on the Board (new _js_string: JS String() of a JSON value).
3. Both routes read the outcome as String(op.outcome ?? "released") and the error
   as String(op.error ?? outcome): an explicit null outcome is a plain release
   (release_op refused it), "" / 0 / false stay themselves and are invalid
   (FakeHub.leases defaulted them to released), an explicit "" error is kept.
   release_op's breaker limit is row.max_retries ?? (Number(failure_limit) ?? 2)
   as recordTaskFailure (max_retries 0 fell through `or` to 2).

Ground truth: node evaluated every expected value in the new tests
(Number(...), String(...), String(x ?? "released")); the Board's '' / null outcome
behaviour is read off releaseTask line 1172 (`String(op.outcome ?? "released")`).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_rejections.py gains Number()/String()
tables, block_kind coercion, outcome/error nullish cases on both routes and the
recordTaskFailure limit; RED on the old fake, GREEN on the new.
